---
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../data/site';
const updated = new Date(LEGAL_UPDATED).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
---
<PageLayout title="Terms of Use – PDFSherpa" description="The terms for using PDFSherpa’s free in-browser PDF and image tools: acceptable use, your responsibilities, open-source license and disclaimers." h1="Terms of Use" path="/terms"
  lead={`Last updated: ${updated}. By using PDFSherpa you agree to these terms. They’re short, and written to be read.`}>
  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>PDFSherpa provides free tools that run in your web browser to edit, convert and compress PDF and image files. Processing happens on your device; we don’t receive or store your files.</p>

  <h2>2. Your files and responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must have the right to use and modify the files you process.</li>
    <li>Don’t use PDFSherpa to infringe copyright, forge documents, mislead others, or break the law.</li>
    <li>Always keep a copy of your originals and check results before relying on them, especially before submitting official applications.</li>
    <li>PDFSherpa won’t remove or bypass passwords or other protection on documents, and you agree not to attempt to make it do so.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    PDFSherpa is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose.
    We do our best, but we can’t guarantee that every file will process correctly, that a size target can be reached, or that an output will be
    accepted by a third-party website.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, PDFSherpa and its contributors aren’t liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for loss of
    data, opportunities or profits, arising from your use of the service. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Open-source license</h2>
  <p>
    PDFSherpa’s source code is free software under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html" rel="noopener">GNU Affero General Public License v3.0</a>.
    It includes third-party components under their own licenses, including Ghostscript (AGPL-3.0), pdf.js (Apache-2.0), pdf-lib (MIT) and JSZip (MIT).
    These terms govern use of the hosted website and don’t restrict your rights under those licenses.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Ads and third parties</h2>
  <p>The site shows ads from Google AdSense and links to other websites. We’re not responsible for third-party content or practices. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms or change or discontinue tools at any time. Continued use after changes means you accept the updated terms.</p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p><EmailLink /></p>
</PageLayout>
